<h2 id="includes">What This Service Includes</h2>
<p>Getting a provider ready to deliver a regenerative program is part paperwork, part process, and part making sure nothing falls through the cracks. We manage the onboarding and readiness work so it's complete, documented, and defensible.</p>

<h3>What We Handle</h3>
<div class="dash-list">
  <div class="dash-list-item">Provider onboarding into the regenerative program</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Privileging aligned to the services being delivered</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Licensing support and documentation</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Operational readiness so providers can start on solid footing</div>
</div>

<h2 id="onboarding">Onboarding &amp; Privileging</h2>
<p>Onboarding a provider into a regenerative program means more than adding a name to a schedule. Privileging has to match the services actually being delivered, the training has to be documented, and the record has to be complete. We coordinate that process so each provider is properly credentialed for the work in front of them.</p>

<h2 id="readiness">Operational Readiness</h2>
<p>Credentialing connects directly to how the program runs. A provider is only truly ready when their onboarding lines up with the protocol, the documentation, and the workflow they'll be working inside. We make sure those pieces fit together rather than being handled in isolation.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Why this matters</div>
  <p class="callout-body">Gaps in credentialing and provider documentation are exactly the kind of thing that surfaces at the worst possible moment — during an audit or a coverage question. Handling it correctly up front means it isn't a problem later.</p>
</div>

